# Secrets. carrier/.gitignore already excludes carrier/.env; repeated here so the
# rule survives that file being moved or rewritten. A live Featherless API key
# lives in carrier/.env — it must never reach a remote, private or otherwise.
.env
*.env
!*.env.example

# Dependencies and build output
node_modules/
website/zariia.tar

# Audio: releases and working files are carried by hand, not by git
*.flac
*.opus
*.ecdc
*.wav

# One exception: the demo record IS the site. It is offered on the player page, the
# build refuses to ship without it, and its key is printed on that page — so it is
# published material, not a release. Keeping it out of git would mean the repo alone
# cannot produce a working deploy.
!website/demo/zariia-demo.flac

# Keys and anything generated that opens a record
SAMPLE-KEY.txt
*.key
*.pem

# macOS
.DS_Store

# ── Held back from the remote on purpose (Prayas, 28 July 2026) ────────────
# Not junk. These are deliberate exclusions, so they are listed here rather
# than merely left unstaged — an ignore rule survives a later `git add -A`,
# a habit does not.
#
#   process-tracker.md   internal; the tracker's own header says it is never
#                        published, never quoted outward, never shown to a
#                        participant
#   archive-shutdown-tool/  the retired scope, kept for reference. Reading it
#                        as current would reintroduce a position that was set
#                        down deliberately
#   funding.md           funding strategy, IFA/Goethe/Pro Helvetia, FCRA and
#                        the open Koher fiscal-sponsorship question
#   movd.md              Museum of Vestigial Desire archive, 468 KB, a
#                        different project that happens to live in this folder
docs/process-tracker.md
docs/archive-shutdown-tool/
docs/funding.md
movd.md
